WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.821
Part four point seven point three.

2
00:00:02.137 --> 00:00:04.297
Dot products: the arithmetic inside

3
00:00:04.297 --> 00:00:04.824
attention.

4
00:00:08.773 --> 00:00:11.255
We are inside attention, the stage where a

5
00:00:11.255 --> 00:00:13.517
slot looks back over the slots before it.

6
00:00:13.848 --> 00:00:16.220
In part four point seven point one, each

7
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.481
slot became a list of ninety-six numbers.

8
00:00:18.812 --> 00:00:21.184
Attention makes shorter lists from them,

9
00:00:21.184 --> 00:00:23.225
twenty-four numbers each in one head.

10
00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.927
Parts four point seven point five and four

11
00:00:25.927 --> 00:00:27.582
point seven point six say how.

12
00:00:27.913 --> 00:00:30.174
Then it keeps asking one question of two

13
00:00:30.174 --> 00:00:31.884
such lists: do they agree?

14
00:00:32.215 --> 00:00:34.697
The answer it uses is a single number, the

15
00:00:34.697 --> 00:00:35.359
dot product.

16
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.952
This part builds it, with no attention

17
00:00:37.952 --> 00:00:39.992
yet: just arrows and arithmetic.

18
00:00:43.373 --> 00:00:45.386
A vector is a list of numbers, in order.

19
00:00:45.673 --> 00:00:47.830
With two numbers we can draw one: three

20
00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.650
along and one up is an arrow from the

21
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.657
centre to that point.

22
00:00:50.944 --> 00:00:51.423
Call it a.

23
00:00:51.711 --> 00:00:54.011
Here is a second, b: one along, two up.

24
00:00:54.298 --> 00:00:56.263
Ninety-six numbers can't be drawn, but

25
00:00:56.263 --> 00:00:58.275
everything we find with two will hold for

26
00:00:58.275 --> 00:00:59.186
any number of them.

27
00:01:02.043 --> 00:01:04.227
The dot product of a and b is written a

28
00:01:04.227 --> 00:01:04.555
dot b.

29
00:01:04.883 --> 00:01:07.012
Multiply the first entries together,

30
00:01:07.012 --> 00:01:09.415
multiply the second entries together, and

31
00:01:09.415 --> 00:01:10.343
add the products.

32
00:01:10.671 --> 00:01:13.183
For our two: three times one, plus one

33
00:01:13.183 --> 00:01:14.165
times two, five.

34
00:01:14.493 --> 00:01:16.186
Two lists in, one number out.

35
00:01:16.657 --> 00:01:17.710
That's the whole recipe.

36
00:01:17.974 --> 00:01:19.028
But what does five mean?

37
00:01:19.291 --> 00:01:21.574
To see it, we need two more ideas: length,

38
00:01:21.574 --> 00:01:22.013
and angle.

39
00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:25.725
How long is a?

40
00:01:25.976 --> 00:01:27.564
Its arrow is the long side of a right

41
00:01:27.564 --> 00:01:29.110
triangle: three along, one up.

42
00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.324
Pythagoras: the length is the square root

43
00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.745
of three squared plus one squared.

44
00:01:32.996 --> 00:01:34.751
The square root of ten, three point one

45
00:01:34.751 --> 00:01:35.085
six two.

46
00:01:35.336 --> 00:01:37.132
And three squared plus one squared is just

47
00:01:37.132 --> 00:01:39.054
a dot a: a vector's length is the square

48
00:01:39.054 --> 00:01:40.559
root of its dot product with itself.

49
00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:42.857
b's length, the same way: the square root

50
00:01:42.857 --> 00:01:44.319
of five, two point two three six.

51
00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.360
The angle between the two arrows is

52
00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.515
forty-five degrees.

53
00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.190
The cosine of an angle is one at zero

54
00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:53.986
degrees, zero at a right angle, and minus

55
00:01:53.986 --> 00:01:56.418
one when the arrows point opposite ways.

56
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:59.275
The cosine of forty-five degrees is zero

57
00:01:59.275 --> 00:02:00.917
point seven zero seven one.

58
00:02:01.937 --> 00:02:04.547
Now a second way to get the dot product:

59
00:02:04.547 --> 00:02:07.043
the length of a, times the length of b,

60
00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:09.199
times the cosine of the angle between

61
00:02:09.199 --> 00:02:09.483
them.

62
00:02:09.823 --> 00:02:12.263
Three point one six two, times two point

63
00:02:12.263 --> 00:02:14.816
two three six, times zero point seven zero

64
00:02:14.816 --> 00:02:16.008
seven one: five.

65
00:02:16.348 --> 00:02:18.277
The same five we got pair by pair.

66
00:02:18.789 --> 00:02:20.273
Why do the two ways agree?

67
00:02:20.615 --> 00:02:22.840
Drop b's shadow straight onto a's line.

68
00:02:23.182 --> 00:02:25.921
Its length is b's length times the cosine:

69
00:02:25.921 --> 00:02:27.347
one point five eight one.

70
00:02:28.279 --> 00:02:30.222
Now turn the whole picture until a lies

71
00:02:30.222 --> 00:02:30.465
flat.

72
00:02:30.756 --> 00:02:32.845
Turning changes the entries, but not the

73
00:02:32.845 --> 00:02:34.934
lengths, not the angle, and, you can

74
00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.343
check, not the dot product.

75
00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:38.723
Now a is three point one six two along and

76
00:02:38.723 --> 00:02:39.112
zero up.

77
00:02:39.403 --> 00:02:41.687
Pair by pair, the up parts meet a zero, so

78
00:02:41.687 --> 00:02:43.775
a dot b is just a's length times b's along

79
00:02:43.775 --> 00:02:45.767
part, and b's along part is its shadow.

80
00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.519
Keep a fixed and swing b around.

81
00:02:51.845 --> 00:02:54.454
Point b the same way as a, half as long:

82
00:02:54.454 --> 00:02:56.736
three times one and a half plus one times

83
00:02:56.736 --> 00:02:57.551
a half, five.

84
00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.160
Turn b to a right angle: three minus

85
00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:00.921
three, zero.

86
00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.605
The pairs cancel exactly.

87
00:03:02.931 --> 00:03:05.214
Point b the opposite way: minus five.

88
00:03:05.683 --> 00:03:08.236
So the sign reads like agreement: positive

89
00:03:08.236 --> 00:03:10.628
when the arrows lean the same way, zero at

90
00:03:10.628 --> 00:03:12.755
right angles, negative when they lean

91
00:03:12.755 --> 00:03:13.074
apart.

92
00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:17.849
Look at two arrows we've met.

93
00:03:18.175 --> 00:03:20.026
The short one along a scored five.

94
00:03:20.353 --> 00:03:22.639
The longer one at forty-five degrees also

95
00:03:22.639 --> 00:03:23.293
scored five.

96
00:03:23.619 --> 00:03:26.232
The dot product mixes two things: how long

97
00:03:26.232 --> 00:03:28.573
the arrows are, and which way they point.

98
00:03:29.125 --> 00:03:31.276
To keep only the direction, divide the dot

99
00:03:31.276 --> 00:03:32.424
product by both lengths.

100
00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.909
That's the cosine similarity: the cosine

101
00:03:34.909 --> 00:03:36.152
of the angle between them.

102
00:03:36.439 --> 00:03:38.686
For the arrow at forty-five degrees: five

103
00:03:38.686 --> 00:03:40.550
over three point one six two times two

104
00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.701
point two three six, zero point seven zero

105
00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:43.179
seven one.

106
00:03:43.466 --> 00:03:45.569
For the short arrow along a: five over

107
00:03:45.569 --> 00:03:47.481
three point one six two times one point

108
00:03:47.481 --> 00:03:49.059
five eight one: exactly one.

109
00:03:50.189 --> 00:03:52.159
Cosine similarity always lies between

110
00:03:52.159 --> 00:03:53.092
minus one and one.

111
00:03:53.403 --> 00:03:54.595
One: the same way.

112
00:03:54.906 --> 00:03:56.306
Zero: at right angles.

113
00:03:56.617 --> 00:03:57.913
Minus one: opposite.

114
00:03:58.224 --> 00:04:00.350
Our forty-five degree arrow sits at zero

115
00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:01.180
point seven one.

116
00:04:01.491 --> 00:04:03.357
The model itself uses the plain dot

117
00:04:03.357 --> 00:04:05.949
product, length and all; cosine similarity

118
00:04:05.949 --> 00:04:08.127
is for us, to read how much two vectors

119
00:04:08.127 --> 00:04:08.438
agree.

120
00:04:11.833 --> 00:04:13.913
With three numbers the arrow lives in a

121
00:04:13.913 --> 00:04:16.202
room instead of on a page, and past three

122
00:04:16.202 --> 00:04:17.450
we can't draw it at all.

123
00:04:17.762 --> 00:04:19.634
But the arithmetic never needed the

124
00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:20.050
picture.

125
00:04:20.362 --> 00:04:22.754
Pair by pair: two times one, minus one

126
00:04:22.754 --> 00:04:24.314
times four, three times two.

127
00:04:24.626 --> 00:04:26.758
Two, minus four, plus six: four.

128
00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:29.202
Length is still Pythagoras, with three

129
00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:31.803
squares: the root of fourteen, three point

130
00:04:31.803 --> 00:04:33.571
seven four two, and the root of

131
00:04:33.571 --> 00:04:35.755
twenty-one, four point five eight three.

132
00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:38.147
Cosine similarity: four over their

133
00:04:38.147 --> 00:04:40.643
product, zero point two three: they lean

134
00:04:40.643 --> 00:04:42.983
the same way a little, about seventy-seven

135
00:04:42.983 --> 00:04:43.711
degrees apart.

136
00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.990
Now two real vectors from T128, our

137
00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:51.247
transformer, on the worked slot that runs

138
00:04:51.247 --> 00:04:53.709
through this whole module: validation song

139
00:04:53.709 --> 00:04:55.916
zero zero one one b three c f, slot five

140
00:04:55.916 --> 00:04:58.122
hundred and seventy-six, the downbeat of

141
00:04:58.122 --> 00:04:58.891
bar thirty-six.

142
00:04:59.199 --> 00:05:01.251
This is a vector of twenty-four numbers

143
00:05:01.251 --> 00:05:03.406
the model made from slot five hundred and

144
00:05:03.406 --> 00:05:05.612
seventy-six, called its query, in head

145
00:05:05.612 --> 00:05:06.843
zero of the first block.

146
00:05:07.151 --> 00:05:09.357
Part four point seven point five says what

147
00:05:09.357 --> 00:05:11.666
a query is, and four point seven point six

148
00:05:11.666 --> 00:05:13.821
what a head is and why it has twenty-four

149
00:05:13.821 --> 00:05:15.154
numbers, not ninety-six.

150
00:05:15.462 --> 00:05:17.309
And this one it made from slot five

151
00:05:17.309 --> 00:05:19.413
hundred and seventy-three, three slots

152
00:05:19.413 --> 00:05:20.644
earlier, called a key.

153
00:05:20.952 --> 00:05:23.260
Multiply them pair by pair: twenty-four

154
00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:23.722
products.

155
00:05:24.143 --> 00:05:26.408
The biggest is entry fifteen, counting

156
00:05:26.408 --> 00:05:29.060
from zero: two point eight five four times

157
00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:31.270
six point seven eight eight, nineteen

158
00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:32.265
point three seven.

159
00:05:32.596 --> 00:05:34.641
Add all twenty-four, positives and

160
00:05:34.641 --> 00:05:36.961
negatives: thirty-one point one nine.

161
00:05:37.473 --> 00:05:39.746
Their lengths are seven point nine three

162
00:05:39.746 --> 00:05:42.074
six and sixteen point two three, so the

163
00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:44.347
cosine similarity is zero point two four.

164
00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:47.230
They lean the same way a little; the dot

165
00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:49.614
product is large partly because the key is

166
00:05:49.614 --> 00:05:49.891
long.

167
00:05:51.554 --> 00:05:53.757
Do the same against other slots' keys.

168
00:05:54.105 --> 00:05:55.845
Against slot five hundred and

169
00:05:55.845 --> 00:05:58.164
seventy-six's own key, minus fourteen

170
00:05:58.164 --> 00:05:59.208
point seven seven.

171
00:05:59.556 --> 00:06:01.295
Against slot five hundred and

172
00:06:01.295 --> 00:06:03.557
seventy-five, one slot back, minus

173
00:06:03.557 --> 00:06:05.296
forty-three point three eight.

174
00:06:05.937 --> 00:06:08.415
In the next part, this number becomes how

175
00:06:08.415 --> 00:06:10.612
much one slot is interested in another.

176
00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:13.429
Here, slot five hundred and seventy-six's

177
00:06:13.429 --> 00:06:15.513
query agrees far more with slot five

178
00:06:15.513 --> 00:06:17.766
hundred and seventy-three than with its

179
00:06:17.766 --> 00:06:19.569
own slot or the one just before.

180
00:06:21.138 --> 00:06:22.913
Say it in one breath: a dot product

181
00:06:22.913 --> 00:06:24.732
multiplies two vectors entry by entry and

182
00:06:24.732 --> 00:06:25.512
adds the products.

183
00:06:25.772 --> 00:06:27.634
It equals one length times the other times

184
00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:29.496
the cosine of the angle between them, so

185
00:06:29.496 --> 00:06:31.445
it is large when they agree, zero at right

186
00:06:31.445 --> 00:06:33.133
angles, and negative when they point

187
00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:33.393
apart.

188
00:06:33.653 --> 00:06:35.169
This pairs with step one of lesson

189
00:06:35.169 --> 00:06:36.728
seventeen in part two of the course

190
00:06:36.728 --> 00:06:37.767
